WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.338
Shivaar, this is the MAD700 scope,
rebuilt from zero.

00:00:05.458 --> 00:00:09.358
Mr Siyah's five pointers in order:
whiteboard first,

00:00:09.478 --> 00:00:12.480
a comment on every line, then a
real run.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.731
Then seven CA-style TODO
questions.

00:00:15.851 --> 00:00:17.802
Have your exam pad ready.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.641
Pointer one.

00:00:20.761 --> 00:00:24.213
An Activity is the brain: one
screen's Java.

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:27.377
The layout is the face: the XML.

00:00:27.497 --> 00:00:30.907
An Intent is the messenger that
opens another screen.

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:32.999
A View is one widget.

00:00:33.119 --> 00:00:35.348
A ViewGroup arranges Views.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.743
match_parent fills the parent,

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:40.265
wrap_content is just big enough.

00:00:40.385 --> 00:00:43.407
Padding is inside, margin is
outside.

00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:46.680
dp for sizes, sp for text.

00:00:47.825 --> 00:00:49.797
onCreate runs first.

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:54.054
Call super, then setContentView to
load the XML.

00:00:54.174 --> 00:00:58.032
findViewById before that returns
null and crashes.

00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:00.318
That bug was in the re-test.

00:01:00.438 --> 00:01:03.076
A click listener runs on every
tap.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.433
An explicit Intent names the exact
class.

00:01:06.553 --> 00:01:10.584
putExtra attaches data,
startActivity opens it,

00:01:10.704 --> 00:01:13.536
and getIntExtra reads it with a
default.

00:01:14.658 --> 00:01:19.053
Boundary value analysis, study
guide page 203:

00:01:19.173 --> 00:01:21.832
find each limit and test each
side.

00:01:21.952 --> 00:01:26.582
For one to ninety-nine: zero, one,
two, ninety-eight,

00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:28.998
ninety-nine, one hundred.

00:01:30.158 --> 00:01:33.568
A real run: zero and one hundred
are rejected,

00:01:33.688 --> 00:01:35.380
the rest accepted.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.143
Today's birthday is accepted,
tomorrow's rejected.

00:01:40.283 --> 00:01:41.974
Pointer two.

00:01:42.094 --> 00:01:46.167
A RelativeLayout places children
relative to the parent or

00:01:46.287 --> 00:01:47.966
other views.

00:01:48.086 --> 00:01:51.003
The study guide says
alignParentLeft,

00:01:51.123 --> 00:01:53.609
the cheat sheet alignParentStart.

00:01:53.729 --> 00:01:55.419
Know both.

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:59.076
The nested horizontal LinearLayout
is the button bar,

00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:00.858
pinned to the bottom.

00:02:00.978 --> 00:02:04.494
Zero dp plus weight one shares the
width equally.

00:02:04.614 --> 00:02:07.037
include pastes in another file.

00:02:07.157 --> 00:02:08.848
Its root is merge,

00:02:08.968 --> 00:02:12.421
so the Save button joins the bar
with no extra layer.

00:02:12.541 --> 00:02:15.027
At plus id creates an id.

00:02:15.147 --> 00:02:17.186
At id refers to one.

00:02:18.325 --> 00:02:21.992
A real check of the actual files:
all eleven parse,

00:02:22.112 --> 00:02:24.599
and the attributes are where we
put them.

00:02:25.742 --> 00:02:27.419
Pointer three.

00:02:27.539 --> 00:02:30.114
The manifest is the app's
passport.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.657
Every Activity must be listed,

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:35.351
or the app crashes when it opens
it.

00:02:35.471 --> 00:02:39.417
The launcher has the intent
filter: MAIN, the first screen,

00:02:39.537 --> 00:02:42.175
and LAUNCHER, the app-drawer icon.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.503
Only one Activity gets it.

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:48.266
Versions live in build dot gradle,
defaultConfig.

00:02:48.386 --> 00:02:51.430
versionCode is an integer for the
Play Store.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.103
versionName is text for the user.

00:02:55.242 --> 00:02:57.407
Now Fragments, slowly.

00:02:57.527 --> 00:03:00.123
The Activity is a frame on the
wall,

00:03:00.243 --> 00:03:02.623
with an empty container inside.

00:03:02.743 --> 00:03:06.411
A Fragment is a removable picture
that slots into that

00:03:06.531 --> 00:03:08.221
container.

00:03:08.341 --> 00:03:11.021
It has its own XML and Java,

00:03:11.141 --> 00:03:13.907
but it always lives inside an
Activity.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:18.506
The FragmentManager swaps them:
begin, replace, commit.

00:03:18.626 --> 00:03:20.812
No commit, no change.

00:03:20.932 --> 00:03:25.133
onCreateView inflates the
Fragment's XML and must return

00:03:25.253 --> 00:03:26.944
that View.

00:03:27.064 --> 00:03:29.850
Fragments are light review on the
pointers,

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.102
but twenty-five marks in both CA
papers.

00:03:34.242 --> 00:03:37.285
The host's layout is one empty
FrameLayout.

00:03:37.405 --> 00:03:41.094
Load HomeFragment only if
savedInstanceState is null,

00:03:41.214 --> 00:03:42.905
the first start.

00:03:43.025 --> 00:03:46.026
After rotation, Android restores
it,

00:03:46.146 --> 00:03:48.699
so loading again makes a
duplicate.

00:03:48.819 --> 00:03:51.393
onCreateView inflates with false,

00:03:51.513 --> 00:03:54.300
and finds the button on the
inflated view.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.058
On a tap: replace with Profile,

00:03:57.178 --> 00:04:00.330
addToBackStack so Back returns,
commit.

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:02.126
Return the view.

00:04:03.283 --> 00:04:05.964
The model: Home, then Profile.

00:04:06.084 --> 00:04:07.774
Back brings Home.

00:04:07.894 --> 00:04:11.604
Back again, with nothing
remembered, closes the screen.

00:04:12.742 --> 00:04:16.022
A DialogFragment is a Fragment
that pops up.

00:04:16.142 --> 00:04:19.764
To send the answer back, it uses a
listener interface:

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:22.028
a phone line with one method.

00:04:22.148 --> 00:04:24.399
The Activity implements it.

00:04:24.519 --> 00:04:27.372
The dialog calls it, then
dismisses.

00:04:28.492 --> 00:04:31.772
Study guide pages sixty-eight and
sixty-nine.

00:04:31.892 --> 00:04:34.808
One: extends DialogFragment.

00:04:34.928 --> 00:04:36.945
Two: the interface.

00:04:37.065 --> 00:04:39.446
Three: an empty constructor.

00:04:39.566 --> 00:04:42.419
Four: inflate and find on the
view.

00:04:42.539 --> 00:04:45.219
Five: OK calls saveItem.

00:04:45.339 --> 00:04:49.540
Six: parse the number, cast
getActivity to the listener,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.589
call it, dismiss.

00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:53.575
The arrow is a lambda;

00:04:53.695 --> 00:04:56.460
the long OnClickListener form
works too.

00:04:57.617 --> 00:05:01.239
The Activity implements the
listener: that's the promise.

00:05:01.359 --> 00:05:04.702
show with the FragmentManager and
a tag opens it.

00:05:04.822 --> 00:05:07.996
The dialog calls
didFinishPortionDialog,

00:05:08.116 --> 00:05:10.433
and the Activity shows the number.

00:05:11.575 --> 00:05:15.884
The model: four typed, four
received, dialog dismissed.

00:05:16.004 --> 00:05:19.305
And all the Android files in your
code folder compile

00:05:19.425 --> 00:05:21.676
against stubs with no errors.

00:05:21.796 --> 00:05:24.240
That checks the code, not a phone.

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.044
Pointer four.

00:05:27.164 --> 00:05:30.295
Four parts: RecyclerView, the
glass.

00:05:30.415 --> 00:05:32.496
The Adapter, the engine.

00:05:32.616 --> 00:05:34.739
The ViewHolder, the cache.

00:05:34.859 --> 00:05:37.346
The LayoutManager stacks rows.

00:05:37.466 --> 00:05:41.282
The row height must be
wrap_content, or you see one row.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:45.346
The ViewHolder finds the row's
views once,

00:05:45.466 --> 00:05:47.155
which stops stutter.

00:05:47.275 --> 00:05:51.475
onCreateViewHolder inflates
item_contact with parent and

00:05:51.595 --> 00:05:53.273
false.

00:05:53.393 --> 00:05:56.545
onBindViewHolder fills the row at
position.

00:05:56.665 --> 00:05:59.924
getItemCount returns size, not
length.

00:06:01.075 --> 00:06:05.857
Wiring: find it, set a
LinearLayoutManager, set the Adapter,

00:06:05.977 --> 00:06:08.442
in onResume so it refreshes.

00:06:08.562 --> 00:06:10.964
Grid: GridLayoutManager.

00:06:11.084 --> 00:06:15.263
After a delete: remove, then
notifyDataSetChanged.

00:06:16.408 --> 00:06:19.709
The model: count three, bind three
rows.

00:06:19.829 --> 00:06:23.367
Remove Ben, notify, and two rows
are bound.

00:06:24.492 --> 00:06:26.182
Pointer five.

00:06:26.302 --> 00:06:29.455
The helper extends
SQLiteOpenHelper.

00:06:29.575 --> 00:06:33.690
super takes the context, the name,
null and the version.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.663
onCreate runs CREATE TABLE once.

00:06:36.783 --> 00:06:39.270
Spell AUTOINCREMENT exactly.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:43.184
Raise the version and onUpgrade
runs: drop the table,

00:06:43.304 --> 00:06:45.322
then onCreate of db.

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:50.093
Insert: ContentValues, column then
value.

00:06:50.213 --> 00:06:53.602
insert returns the row id, or
minus one.

00:06:53.722 --> 00:06:57.602
Reading: moveToFirst, loop while
not isAfterLast,

00:06:57.722 --> 00:07:02.052
read by column index, add,
moveToNext, then close.

00:07:02.172 --> 00:07:04.959
Forget moveToNext and it never
ends.

00:07:05.079 --> 00:07:08.552
For a search, use a question mark
and a String array.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:13.816
The same SQL in real SQLite: new
row ids,

00:07:13.936 --> 00:07:17.924
the question-mark search finds
Ben, delete removes one row,

00:07:18.044 --> 00:07:21.154
and a nameless row is refused by
NOT NULL.

00:07:22.283 --> 00:07:24.449
Your sources disagree here.

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:27.122
Weight: write zero dp.

00:07:27.242 --> 00:07:31.551
Insert: minus one and greater than
zero both mean success.

00:07:31.671 --> 00:07:34.437
Key column: use the skeleton's
name.

00:07:34.557 --> 00:07:36.553
Versions: Gradle.

00:07:36.673 --> 00:07:40.682
And the study guide's chapter
three MCQ one key is wrong.

00:07:41.825 --> 00:07:43.499
Key takeaways.

00:07:43.619 --> 00:07:45.299
Pause and copy them.

00:07:45.419 --> 00:07:47.585
setContentView first.

00:07:47.705 --> 00:07:49.613
Each side of each limit.

00:07:49.733 --> 00:07:52.241
Every Activity in the manifest.

00:07:52.361 --> 00:07:54.784
onCreateView returns the view.

00:07:54.904 --> 00:07:56.900
A listener plus dismiss.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.316
Four roles, three methods.

00:07:59.436 --> 00:08:03.851
AUTOINCREMENT, question marks,
moveToNext, close.

00:08:04.992 --> 00:08:09.171
Your turn: seven CA-style
questions, easy to hard,

00:08:09.291 --> 00:08:10.983
with a countdown.

00:08:11.103 --> 00:08:13.032
Pause longer if you need.

00:08:13.152 --> 00:08:17.140
Question one, easy: explain the
crash, fix it,

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:20.670
read ITEM_COUNT with default zero,
and show it.

00:08:33.825 --> 00:08:35.885
Question two, easy:

00:08:36.005 --> 00:08:39.136
the quantity rule and its six
boundary values.

00:08:52.283 --> 00:08:57.192
Question three, medium, the real
CA question: orientation,

00:08:57.312 --> 00:09:00.422
email, password, and the login
button.

00:09:13.575 --> 00:09:17.327
Question four, medium: the three
Adapter methods.

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:34.566
Question five, hard: the custom
dialog with its listener.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:52.288
Question six, hard, from the re-
test: CREATE TABLE member,

00:09:52.408 --> 00:09:54.098
then the Cursor loop.

00:10:07.242 --> 00:10:11.378
Question seven, hard, from the CA:
load once,

00:10:11.498 --> 00:10:13.470
then navigate with Back.

00:10:26.617 --> 00:10:28.308
Answer one.

00:10:28.428 --> 00:10:32.522
findViewById before setContentView
returned null.

00:10:32.642 --> 00:10:34.324
Swap them.

00:10:34.444 --> 00:10:37.766
Then getIntExtra with zero, and
setText.

00:10:38.908 --> 00:10:40.600
Answer two.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:44.279
Greater-or-equal one, less-or-
equal ninety-nine.

00:10:44.399 --> 00:10:48.366
Zero and one hundred rejected, the
other four accepted.

00:10:49.492 --> 00:10:51.742
Answer three, from the memo.

00:10:51.862 --> 00:10:53.534
Vertical.

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:57.555
textEmailAddress, textPassword,
not password.

00:10:57.675 --> 00:11:00.013
The button has ems ten.

00:11:01.158 --> 00:11:02.850
Answer four.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.571
Inflate with parent and false,
return a ViewHolder.

00:11:06.691 --> 00:11:08.815
Bind getName at position.

00:11:08.935 --> 00:11:10.625
Return size.

00:11:11.783 --> 00:11:13.475
Answer five.

00:11:13.595 --> 00:11:17.689
extends DialogFragment, the
interface, inflate,

00:11:17.809 --> 00:11:20.874
find on the view, OK calls
saveItem.

00:11:20.994 --> 00:11:25.174
Then parse, cast getActivity,
call, dismiss.

00:11:26.325 --> 00:11:28.017
Answer six.

00:11:28.137 --> 00:11:31.653
id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY
AUTOINCREMENT,

00:11:31.773 --> 00:11:35.997
name and plan NOT NULL, monthlyFee
REAL, joinYear INTEGER.

00:11:36.117 --> 00:11:39.718
Then the memo's loop: rawQuery
with a question mark,

00:11:39.838 --> 00:11:43.333
while moveToNext, getString zero,
close.

00:11:44.492 --> 00:11:46.766
Answer seven, from the memo.

00:11:46.886 --> 00:11:50.381
If savedInstanceState is null,
replace and commit.

00:11:50.501 --> 00:11:52.797
Inflate, find on the view.

00:11:52.917 --> 00:11:56.884
On tap: replace, addToBackStack
null, commit.

00:11:57.004 --> 00:11:58.679
Return the view.

00:11:59.825 --> 00:12:01.516
Mark yourself,

00:12:01.636 --> 00:12:05.367
then send me photos of your exam
pad and I'll mark them line

00:12:05.487 --> 00:12:07.168
by line.

00:12:07.288 --> 00:12:10.677
The code folder's README says
where each file goes.

00:12:10.797 --> 00:12:12.748
You've got this, Shivaar.
